Internal Working of Iterator:
-------------------------------

1. You call iterator()
2. Collection returns its
 internal Iterator implementation (private inner class)
3. Iterator uses:
      i.cursor to track current position
      ii.expectedModCount to detect modifications (fail-fast)
4. hasNext() checks if more elements exist
5. next() returns element + moves cursor

